      </article>

      <article class="patent-entry">
        <h3><a href="#">105 &ndash; US 9,705,511 &ndash; Ultra low phase noise frequency synthesizer</a></h3>
        <p>This patent describes a frequency synthesizer that provides ultra-low phase noise output using Fractional-N PLL, Sampling Reference PLL, and DDS techniques. The synthesizer is designed for use in communication systems requiring high modulation schemes and data rates.</p>
        <p>&nbsp;<a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US9705511" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="official-record-link">Official Record &#x2197;</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="patent-entry">
        <h3><a href="#">106 &ndash; US 9,729,158 &ndash; Ultra low phase noise frequency synthesizer</a></h3>
        <p>This patent covers a frequency synthesizer system that reduces phase noise through a combination of PLL and DDS techniques. The design enables communication systems to achieve lower phase deviations, supporting higher-order modulation schemes.</p>
        <p>&nbsp;<a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US9729158" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="official-record-link">Official Record &#x2197;</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="patent-entry">
        <h3><a href="#">107 &ndash; US 9,831,881 &ndash; Radar target detection system for autonomous vehicles with ultra-low phase noise</a></h3>
